{
	"children": [
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "U.S. Route 45 in Michigan"
				}
			],
			"type": "h1",
			"id": "p_4lHuqpBzP2-axDOuCzg"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "\n"
				},
				{
					"text": "US Highway 45",
					"bold": true
				},
				{
					"text": " ("
				},
				{
					"text": "US 45",
					"bold": true
				},
				{
					"text": ") is a part of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "United States Numbered Highway System"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Numbered_Highway_System",
					"id": "qXZtyJ6f0Z4OPNdeEwgAe"
				},
				{
					"text": " that runs from "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Mobile, Alabama"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobile,_Alabama",
					"id": "hKN-eC3Rs_WI2OrZ4cAny"
				},
				{
					"text": ", to the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Upper Peninsula"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upper_Peninsula_of_Michigan",
					"id": "B063-qsWwub8Wchaj35IV"
				},
				{
					"text": " (UP) of the state of "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Michigan"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan",
					"id": "WxUEq-cMhIT3Zl46haiMN"
				},
				{
					"text": ". The highway forms a part of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "state trunkline highway system"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan_State_Trunkline_Highway_System",
					"id": "8fcxfRs2upCUjH75J30zf"
				},
				{
					"text": " that is maintained by the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Michigan Department of Transportation"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan_Department_of_Transportation",
					"id": "8PRSAFxqlfslINQ209jEk"
				},
				{
					"text": " (MDOT). It enters the state from "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Wisconsin"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wisconsin",
					"id": "Cuo8TMZvrGXe_cqVSo0mY"
				},
				{
					"text": " south of "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Watersmeet"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watersmeet,_Michigan",
					"id": "w65sUjBejKZsE5CLc7DTp"
				},
				{
					"text": ", ending at an intersection with Ontonagon Street in "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Ontonagon"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ontonagon,_Michigan",
					"id": "0UpBHLdt0ym33u-hu1ReR"
				},
				{
					"text": ". In between, the roadway crosses the UP running for approximately 54+3⁄4 miles (88.1 km) through the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Ottawa National Forest"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottawa_National_Forest",
					"id": "VYIMqUb5bs5oBtBU0PSEN"
				},
				{
					"text": " and parallel to the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Ontonagon River"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ontonagon_River",
					"id": "bX8PDnoQOwjWmvwM0eEp7"
				},
				{
					"text": "."
				}
			],
			"type": "p",
			"id": "qq7mhYplXXdIqhGCSt2aS"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "The highway dates back to the 1930s in Michigan. At the time it was extended into the state, it replaced sections of "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "M-26"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M-26_(Michigan_highway)",
					"id": "Czcan2ViEZIo3rxYhd3JG"
				},
				{
					"text": " and "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "M-35"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M-35_(Michigan_highway)",
					"id": "v0eyfxf3GubHc232XN_Ig"
				},
				{
					"text": ". An eight-mile (13 km) segment was significantly reconstructed in the late 1950s, and an alignment change in the 1970s moved the routing of US 45 near "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Rockland"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockland,_Michigan",
					"id": "IFLng09yyp2abYXb69Xje"
				},
				{
					"text": " before it was reversed soon afterwards. A segment of roadway that formerly carried US 45 is the site of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Paulding Light"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paulding_Light",
					"id": "RVEgB_BZuAlCAtI877n1J"
				},
				{
					"text": ", a local phenomenon whose origins were scientifically described in 2010."
				}
			],
			"type": "p",
			"id": "wizxrsdXEFpdMlLjKuCpg"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "Route description"
				}
			],
			"id": "G2fBpXWzX2_CmpBYwhR7u",
			"type": "h2"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "US 45 crosses from Wisconsin to Michigan near "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Land O' Lakes, Wisconsin"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_O%27_Lakes,_Wisconsin",
					"id": "YXVrJ-1tEfIbuGJYz9uGF"
				},
				{
					"text": ", east of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Sylvania Wilderness"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sylvania_Wilderness",
					"id": "ZmS2zZLKvT_AR7nx3B6Og"
				},
				{
					"text": " area of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Ottawa National Forest"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottawa_National_Forest",
					"id": "CiD9piQIiVQbqAQJFq3V8"
				},
				{
					"text": ". The highway angles northeast from the state line before curving around to the north toward Watersmeet, where it intersects "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "US 2"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_2_in_Michigan",
					"id": "s6dAtHIqUvAGz5Qq29Py-"
				},
				{
					"text": ". Watersmeet is home to the northern section of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Lac Vieux Desert Indian Reservation"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lac_Vieux_Desert_Indian_Reservation",
					"id": "ET9L_wprgmzY-V3fmqBxw"
				},
				{
					"text": ". Continuing north across the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Gogebic"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gogebic_County,_Michigan",
					"id": "AYWWj-HEnDoVaP6HTFV3t"
				},
				{
					"text": "–"
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Ontonagon"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ontonagon_County,_Michigan",
					"id": "YxGjAm0NN-nmgc_6jhLz9"
				},
				{
					"text": " county line, US 45 crosses the boundary between the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Central"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Time_Zone_(Americas)",
					"id": "nBeUzgZBEGBj-QIIk_YSe"
				},
				{
					"text": " and "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Eastern"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Time_Zone",
					"id": "R2Ag-sc9TBx85LVXf3GUK"
				},
				{
					"text": " time zones."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[4]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-MDOT09-4",
					"id": "nUdi5fDKeoKsv0GyVI2yj"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[5]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-RM08-5",
					"id": "s1mgQ9jl_rZOCRfLkbE0s"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				}
			],
			"type": "p",
			"id": "Ea3ysThSRSMyxC_n9x98P"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "In southern Ontonagon County, the highway runs west of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Bond Falls"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bond_Falls",
					"id": "0NQxh6fZnUEomvyHHvOt3"
				},
				{
					"text": " Flowage near "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Paulding"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paulding,_Michigan",
					"id": "PeVF3X03fKCW16R4m6lHX"
				},
				{
					"text": ". North of here, the trunkline enters "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Bruce Crossing"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruce_Crossing,_Michigan",
					"id": "qK6j3ldNHFVnaUT0Gej7S"
				},
				{
					"text": " and intersects "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "M-28"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M-28_(Michigan_highway)",
					"id": "PzZB-FGmsTCJz9BSO8aTV"
				},
				{
					"text": ". After leaving town, US 45 runs northward parallel to the Middle Branch of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Ontonagon River"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ontonagon_River",
					"id": "KtCBvHxdC_dGv12l85NGx"
				},
				{
					"text": ", and the highway crosses the river near a roadside park south of "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Rockland"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockland,_Michigan",
					"id": "Yb44DxLpvT3CpD01Xgd_k"
				},
				{
					"text": ". East of Rockland, US 45 meets the southern terminus of "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "M-26"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M-26_(Michigan_highway)",
					"id": "ItGPr1hgCT4HGOsbsQFY-"
				},
				{
					"text": "; after the intersection, US 45 turns northwesterly and runs parallel to the Ontonagon River"
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[4]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-MDOT09-4",
					"id": "qCsdPQuFnht56H6kv2e0y"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[5]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-RM08-5",
					"id": "KMXRp41FNibDccC1TwbBo"
				},
				{
					"text": " and a snowmobile trail (a former branch of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Escanaba and Lake Superior Railroad"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escanaba_and_Lake_Superior_Railroad",
					"id": "6PRVIjI1_Jh3_M-9cKucM"
				},
				{
					"text": ")."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[6]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-ashcraft-6",
					"id": "hChuozRGl7f8dsxHnrFS2"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[7]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-7",
					"id": "GQ2bL0dy46aicZN6qdKTQ"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				}
			],
			"type": "p",
			"id": "ghT50dN_pJTmMdHdTm_ba"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "US 45 enters the south side of "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Ontonagon"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ontonagon,_Michigan",
					"id": "-yjyrIvre-2H-L6oQ4THp"
				},
				{
					"text": " on Rockland Road near the Holy Family Cemetery. The roadway turns due north, still running parallel to the course of the river. South of downtown, the highway crosses an intersection that serves as the joint termini of "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "M-38"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M-38_(Michigan_highway)",
					"id": "hezFxbwOmjwHNG65PB33g"
				},
				{
					"text": " and "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "M-64"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M-64_(Michigan_highway)",
					"id": "t2UQIDM0769XfKnQ9o-WB"
				},
				{
					"text": ". M-64 crosses the river from the west on a bridge built in 2006 and ends at the intersection."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[8]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-googleO-8",
					"id": "M7OEzWWuDWNcRSMoh_ktF"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[9]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-ORB-9",
					"id": "WBZmNdI-epR13FsMN40LI"
				},
				{
					"text": " M-38 comes into town from the east and also ends at the same intersection. US 45 continues north on Rockland Road and turns northwest on River Street along the eastern river bank through downtown. The northern terminus of US 45 is at Ontonagon Street, about 1,000 feet (300 m) from "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Lake Superior"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lake_Superior",
					"id": "AUymV04jcww-bD5-EANfJ"
				},
				{
					"text": "."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[8]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-googleO-8",
					"id": "9XWlNXEMWllm5YfSI1D2i"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				}
			],
			"type": "p",
			"id": "njCsdy9sQJ9fU382uMHCb"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "History"
				}
			],
			"id": "vbFlPB23K6Mydgk3urqoT",
			"type": "h2"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "US 45 debuted in Michigan by 1935 on maps of the time. The highway previously terminated in "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Des Plaines, Illinois"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Des_Plaines,_Illinois",
					"id": "6hqdsqrPCR3f0i4UCABoB"
				},
				{
					"text": ", until it was extended northward to Michigan."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[10]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-10",
					"id": "ldF61iMrp_oIQc1r4lSoY"
				},
				{
					"text": " US 45 replaced "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "M-26"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M-26_(Michigan_highway)",
					"id": "yQM7dgRyDztA_9GLSwaLq"
				},
				{
					"text": " between the state line north toward Rockland, as well as "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "M-35"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M-35_(Michigan_highway)",
					"id": "5F4KPIvNo3AJQM8-1R-4u"
				},
				{
					"text": " between Rockland and Ontonagon."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[2]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-MSHD34-09-2",
					"id": "2VG9RsZJq0_Mmf2Mmfl-9"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[3]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-MSHD35-05-3",
					"id": "DGfRyhJyBqUZwdJPDIALG"
				},
				{
					"text": " The "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Michigan State Highway Department"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan_State_Highway_Department",
					"id": "JX20_pPLAQU-1XxH4GrpQ"
				},
				{
					"text": " (MSHD) rebuilt an eight-mile (13 km) section of the highway in the Military Hills area of eastern Ontonagon County starting in 1957. As part of the project, tons of waste copper rock were hauled into the area to provide a base for the reconstructed roadway, which was previously quite steep through the hills and muddy during rains."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[11]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-11",
					"id": "gdm9ENcEi5GB9M1UmXMki"
				},
				{
					"text": " The project included a new bridge over the Ontonagon River that opened in late 1959. Along with this bridge, the last eight miles (13 km) of US 45 in the country were paved, connecting the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Gulf of Mexico"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_of_Mexico",
					"id": "qLhtlCmsD54w1IAhrg4n_"
				},
				{
					"text": " and Lake Superior with a hard-surfaced road."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[12]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-12",
					"id": "d0snhmIrkJ7tIkX5PgHWH"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				}
			],
			"type": "p",
			"id": "wefppWGJXVTH0J2gxLHnk"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "A rerouting in late 1971 moved the US 45 designation along M-26 between Rockland and "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Greenland"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenland,_Michigan",
					"id": "v-NhiIgWQ9g5uA0AZIPMV"
				},
				{
					"text": ". From Greenland, US 45 followed Ontonagon–Greenland Road to Ontonagon."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[13]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-MDSH71-13",
					"id": "bDJfohpUjqBcJq_YiwH2a"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[14]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-MDSH72-14",
					"id": "oqPgZfrkLL8bqqWUgJC8F"
				},
				{
					"text": " In late 1973, MDOT reversed the rerouting—US 45 was restored to its previous routing on Rockland Road between Rockland and Ontonagon and M-26 was re-extended south from Greenland to Rockland; M-38 was extended west along Ontonagon–Greenland Road."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[15]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-MDSH73-15",
					"id": "YN4a5UNDW3a6JWYR1Pkm9"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[16]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-MDSHT74-16",
					"id": "pTQVkRW5t0f7RjGPxmhm6"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				}
			],
			"type": "p",
			"id": "CvQe6JUtc7VV5IviTTUQv"
		},
		{
			"children": [
				{
					"text": "In 2010, students from "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Michigan Technological University"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michigan_Technological_University",
					"id": "R80Kpjc58QjSyQ1GKPPM7"
				},
				{
					"text": " solved the mystery of the "
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "Paulding Light"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paulding_Light",
					"id": "9WB0LWV1UyD2X7P6ouGdC"
				},
				{
					"text": ", a local phenomenon commonly attributed to paranormal activity."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[17]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-DMG2010-17",
					"id": "p6tPs6WjJTYVsBOoLWq1p"
				},
				{
					"text": " The phenomenon is viewable from a section of Robbins Pond Road, the former routing of US 45 in the Paulding area."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[18]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-18",
					"id": "W1dB1SXoS_2v0-QbU_07b"
				},
				{
					"text": " According to area folklore, and indicated on signs in the viewing area, the light is from the ghost of a railroad brakeman. Other explanations say the light comes from a ghost train from the 19th century."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[19]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-19",
					"id": "W78FWQ5p0uyTC6iHCtY-b"
				},
				{
					"text": " The students' investigation showed that the light comes from headlights of cars on US 45 in the Paulding area."
				},
				{
					"children": [
						{
							"text": "[17]"
						}
					],
					"type": "a",
					"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Route_45_in_Michigan#cite_note-DMG2010-17",
					"id": "1gg191wgOq7AMEjjkNdkk"
				},
				{
					"text": ""
				}
			],
			"type": "p",
			"id": "f2GrgzMqmCTvDUvEeygV9"
